<!-- ========================================================================
     DROID_REPAIR_FOR_PROFIT_EVENTS_1 (packet C5).

     RUT_DroidRepairJob reaches the player through the NATURAL RANDOM POOL
     (rootSelectionWeight 1.1, minRefireDays 15) - that is the "regular event"
     ruling 2 asked for, and the frequency cap section 6 demanded.

     This IncidentDef exists at baseChance 0 for one reason: a deterministic
     trigger. skills/rimworld-quests/SKILL.md section 7 - "never gate a
     verification on the storyteller". Fire it from dev mode (Debug actions ->
     Do incident) or a bridge call to force the quest to offer, instead of
     waiting for a roll. Same shape as VaultDungeons' RUT_GiveQuest_* row.

     baseChance 0 also means it can never double the natural pool's own rate.
======================================================================== -->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef ParentName="GiveQuestBase">
    <defName>RUT_GiveQuest_DroidRepairJob</defName>
    <label>quest: droid repair job</label>
    <letterLabel>Quest available</letterLabel>
    <questScriptDef>RUT_DroidRepairJob</questScriptDef>
    <baseChance>0</baseChance>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
